{
  "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8062-97dd-fbe53495315a",
  "title": "REST controllers and request mapping",
  "sourceUrl": "https://xpandeyed.notion.site/20824eb1ed54806297ddfbe53495315a",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-0",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring MVC controllers"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-mvc-full-form",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "MVC stands for Model\u2013View\u2013Controller."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-0-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring MVC is the Spring Framework module that connects incoming requests to controller methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-0-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The "
        ],
        [
          "spring-boot-starter-web",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " dependency supplies Spring MVC and the embedded servlet server for these examples."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-0-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot configures the MVC infrastructure when that dependency is present."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-0-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A controller is a Spring bean with methods that Spring MVC can call for matching requests."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-0-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@RestController",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " registers the class as a controller and treats method return values as response data."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-0-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A controller method that handles a request is called a handler method."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-0-note-6",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Controllers use the component scanning and constructor injection already explained in the bean lessons."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Request mappings"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-1-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@RequestMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " on a class declares a shared path for its handler methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-1-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@GetMapping",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " on a method declares the path that method handles for "
        ],
        [
          "GET",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " requests."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-1-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring combines the class path and the method path."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-1-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring records these mappings during application startup."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-1-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "For a matching request, Spring calls the method on the controller bean. Application code does not call that method to receive the request."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-1-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Map a request to a greeting controller",
        "language": "java",
        "description": [
          "Each example is a separate project. All required application files appear in the tabs.",
          "`GreetingController.java` belongs in `src/main/java/com/example/demo/` beside `DemoApplication`.",
          "The application restarts after the files change.",
          "The server uses port `8080` in the command. A configured port replaces it.",
          "`mvn spring-boot:run` starts the application from the directory containing `pom.xml`. Requests run in a second terminal."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "Spring discovers both beans and injects `GreetingService` into `GreetingController`.",
          "`@RequestMapping` supplies `/greetings` and `@GetMapping` supplies `/hello`.",
          "Spring calls `hello()` when it receives `GET /greetings/hello`.",
          "The controller calls the service with `Ada`.",
          "`@RestController` makes the returned `String` response text.",
          "A separate repository is unnecessary because this operation does not read or save data."
        ],
        "commands": "curl http://localhost:8080/greetings/hello",
        "result": "Hello, Ada",
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/GreetingController.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestMapping;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;\n\n@RestController\n@RequestMapping(\"/greetings\")\npublic class GreetingController {\n    private final GreetingService service;\n\n    public GreetingController(GreetingService service) {\n        this.service = service;\n    }\n\n    @GetMapping(\"/hello\")\n    public String hello() {\n        return service.greet(\"Ada\");\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/GreetingFormatter.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Component;\n\n@Component\npublic class GreetingFormatter {\n    public String format(String name) {\n        return \"Hello, \" + name;\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/GreetingService.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\n\n@Service\npublic class GreetingService {\n    private final GreetingFormatter formatter;\n\n    public GreetingService(GreetingFormatter formatter) {\n        this.formatter = formatter;\n    }\n\n    public String greet(String name) {\n        return formatter.format(name);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-2",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Response data and views"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-2-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@RestController",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " combines "
        ],
        [
          "@Controller",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "@ResponseBody",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-2-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@Controller",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " without "
        ],
        [
          "@ResponseBody",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " can interpret a returned "
        ],
        [
          "String",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " as a view name."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-2-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The REST controller examples return data rather than view names."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-2-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@RestController",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " does not make every result JSON. A returned "
        ],
        [
          "String",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " normally becomes text."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "restful-web-services-lesson-2-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Request and response bodies explains how Spring converts Java objects to JSON after the lessons on mappings and parameters."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
